Congratulations Mennatullah Siam!

You have been awarded the Alberta Innovates Technology Futures Scholarship
at the University of Alberta. Attached is the offer letter outlining
details of the scholarship. Please read *both* the offer letter and the
body of this email text carefully and follow all instructions within.
Please  submit the appropriate form, as requested in the offer letter.
Graduate Award Acceptance or Decline forms can be submitted electronically,
by fax, or hard copy (by mail or drop off at our office).

*NOTE:  July 15, 2016 is the deadline for award acceptance forms for awards
starting on September 1, 2016 to ensure an end of September payment.
Students whom submit an acceptance form after July 15, 2016 may experience
a delay in payment of their award, although we will make every effort to
pay students on time.   *

*IMPORTANT: At the time of accepting this award, please confirm your
research area for AITF reporting purposes via clicking here
<http://goo.gl/forms/e78U8RogKiOszksJ2>.   *

Please let us know if you have any questions.

Best regards,

Michelle

*PLEASE QUOTE STUDENT ID, IF APPLICABLE*

<http://gradstudies.ualberta.ca>

Award Services

Katya, Ashley, Christine, Emma, Ling, Michelle, Patricia

Faculty of Graduate Studies & Research

2-29 Triffo Hall

University of Alberta

Edmonton, Alberta, Canada T6G 2E1

780-492-9460

gradstudies.ualberta.ca

<http://gradstudies.ualberta.ca/>
Confidentiality Notice: This communication and any attachments are intended
for the use of the recipient to whom it is addressed and may contain;
confidential, personal, and/or privileged information. Please contact me
immediately if you are not the intended recipient of this communication,
and do not copy, distribute, or take any action relying on it. Any
communication received in error, or subsequent reply, should be deleted or
destroyed.

*IMPORTANT: Acceptance and Renewal of September Awards*
Due to cut-off times and a switchover from the legacy graduate awards
solution (GRAD) to the new FGSR Grad Awards solution, all students holding
the awards which are renewable or starting on September 1, 2016 must submit
the appropriate acceptance of renewal documentation to FGSR by July 15,
2016. Students who fail to submit this documentations before July 15 should
expect a delay in payment of their award. Please see here
<https://drive.google.com/a/ualberta.ca/file/d/0B9-kZpxtD1w6RFdRcXlNRmtUY1k/view?usp=sharing>for
more details.

